      "reason": "the section's own filing commit lists \"push by the port-443 route on compute nodes\" as one of its three purposes, so the gate as written certifies two thirds of the deliverable and would let the node close with the recurrence unfixed; adding the case (or dropping the clause) changes the plan text, and the sibling \u00a742 already guards its own skill-text clause with `tests/test_skill_contracts.py`.",
      "text": "the Deliverable requires the push to use the port-443 route on a host where port 22 is refused, and requires the skill's integrate step to say so, but the Done when names exactly two cases (a failed push reported as a landed commit with a distinct exit status, and a rerun pushing without a second merge) plus one base-tree negative control, so the only clause that stops the compute-node push from failing at all is unmeasured and a worker can satisfy the whole gate while shipping neither the fallback nor the skill text",
